  "text": "A classic breakfast omelette is a simple yet versatile dish that can be tailored to personal preferences. To prepare the perfect omelette, start by cracking 2 to 3 eggs into a bowl and whisking them together until the yolk and white are fully blended. Next, season with a pinch of salt and pepper to enhance the flavor. Add a splash of milk to create a fluffier consistency, and stir in a small amount of butter to add richness. Heat a non-stick pan over medium heat, then pour the egg mixture into the pan. As the eggs begin to set, use a spatula to gently lift and fold the edges toward the center. Once the omelette is cooked through but still slightly underdone, place a spoonful of cheese in the center and carefully fold the omelette in half. Cook for a few more moments until the cheese is melted and the omelette is fully cooked. Before serving, garnish with fresh herbs or vegetables for a delightful touch.",
